{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA plan-review finding, once surfaced, can replay verbatim on every later review of the same\nticket even after the plan is edited to fully address it, so the revise-review loop never\nconverges and each round costs a full LLM review. Confirmed on epic `0e68-41eb-5782-4336`,\nwhere one G6 finding blocked five consecutive rounds. The root cause is recorded in full on\nthis ticket's first comment; the load-bearing evidence is summarised below.\n\n## Approach\n\n`sidecar.prior_concerns` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py`) selects prior findings for\nre-surfacing on `decision in {\"block\",\"advisory\"}` and `priority >= RECALL_MIN_PRIORITY`\nalone. `pass1.run_pass1` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py`, the \"Recall\" block after the\nISF pass) then injects each one with a hardcoded `\"evidence\": []` and `\"impact\": \"\"`. Because\n`sidecar.build_payload._slim` persists an explicit allow-list that does not include the\n`_recall` marker, a re-surfaced finding is re-verified, re-decided `block`, and re-persisted\nindistinguishably from a fresh one — so it re-qualifies for recall every round. Recall was\nbuilt as a one-shot backstop for a finder that MISSED a finding on identical material\n(`sidecar.py`, the recall section comment) and instead behaves as a permanent ratchet.\n\nThe designed Pass-2 backstop does not fire because the injected candidate carries no\ngrounding: `review_kernel/verify.finding_listing` renders `evidence:` as an empty string, so\n`evidence_entails_finding` has nothing to test, and the absence veto in\n`review_kernel/decide.py` (`claims_absence == \"yes\"` AND `absence_confirmed_in_context ==\n\"no\"`) never fires because the verifier confirms the bare restatement instead of searching the\ncurrent plan for the refuting provision. Verified on the epic's final sidecar: the blocking\nfinding recorded `claims_absence: \"yes\"`, `absence_confirmed_in_context: \"yes\"`, `evidence:\n[]`, while `orchestrator.assemble_context(...).plan_text` (7568 chars, in the verifier's\ncontext via `prompts.shared_plan_prefix`) contains the refuting provision verbatim.\n\nThe fix keeps all three changes inside the recall eligibility/injection path so fresh-finding\nverification is untouched:\n\n1. `prior_concerns` carries the prior finding's persisted `evidence` (and `impact`) into the\n   concern, and `run_pass1` injects them instead of blanking them. v2 sidecars already persist\n   `evidence` losslessly (`build_payload._slim`); `prior_concerns` simply never read it. This\n   is the re-grounding: Pass-2 now judges the original quotes against the CURRENT plan text\n   rather than rubber-stamping an assertion with nothing behind it.\n2. A prior finding with no persisted grounding evidence is INELIGIBLE for recall — there is\n   nothing to re-ground it with. That set is exactly the previous recall injections, so this\n   breaks the ratchet, and it works against already-written sidecars with no migration.\n3. Recall is suppressed wholesale when the prior sidecar's `material_fingerprint` differs from\n   `attest.current_material_fingerprint(ticket_id, repo_root=...)`. On CHANGED material the\n   fresh finder's silence is evidence the edit resolved the finding, not a miss — which is\n   recall's own stated contract. Both fingerprints must be present for the comparison to\n   apply; a missing one leaves recall enabled (best-effort, as today).\n\nWhy this shape rather than a new LLM re-grounding sub-call: the sidecars already record every\nsignal needed (`evidence`, `material_fingerprint`), so the gap closes deterministically at\nzero additional token cost and stays unit-testable without a model. A genuinely unaddressed\ngap still blocks, because the fresh Pass-1 finder re-emits it with real evidence on the\nchanged plan (observed on the epic: the finding was found fresh with 3 evidence items while it\nwas genuinely unaddressed, and only went evidence-empty once the plan was fixed).\n\n`build_payload._slim` additionally persists a `recalled` boolean so the ratchet is visible in\noffline calibration, and `run_pass1` records the suppression reason in `coverage`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py` — `prior_concerns`: carry `evidence`/`impact`,\n  exclude evidence-less priors, add the material-fingerprint suppression; `build_payload._slim`:\n  persist `recalled`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py` — the recall block: inject the carried\n  `evidence`/`impact`; record the suppression/eligibility counts in `coverage`.\n- `tests/unit/test_pass1_recall.py` — the regression test for the replay scenario, plus fixture\n  updates for the tightened eligibility contract.\n\nNo change to `review_kernel/verify.py`, `review_kernel/decide.py`, the verifier prompts, or any\nfresh-finding path. The completion-verifier work on tickets `1656` and `1700` is on a different\npath (`completion_subcall.py` / `completion_sidecar.py`) and is not touched.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: a prior `block` finding WITH evidence, on UNCHANGED material, is still recalled\n  and now carries its evidence and impact into the injected candidate.\n- The replay regression: a prior `block` finding with `evidence: []` (the signature a previous\n  recall injection leaves) is NOT recalled, so a second review cannot replay it.\n- Changed material: a fully eligible prior finding is NOT recalled when the sidecar's\n  `material_fingerprint` differs from the current one, and IS recalled when they match.\n- Edge/degrade: a sidecar missing `material_fingerprint`, and an `attest` lookup that raises,\n  both leave recall enabled rather than failing the review (the existing best-effort posture,\n  covered by the existing `test_prior_concerns_best_effort_on_reader_error`).\n- Unaffected: `test_finder_never_receives_prior_findings` and\n  `test_recalled_candidate_dropped_by_pass2_when_resolved` continue to pass unchanged, pinning\n  that Pass-1 independence and the Pass-2 validity backstop are not weakened.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The root cause is recorded as a comment on this ticket naming where recall reinjects\n      findings and why plan-text re-grounding is skipped — checked by `rebar show\n      deceitful-flannel-jerboa` showing the comment.\n- [x] A prior finding with no persisted grounding evidence is not returned by\n      `sidecar.prior_concerns` — checked by a new unit test in `tests/unit/test_pass1_recall.py`\n      asserting the evidence-less concern is absent from the result while an\n      evidence-carrying sibling is present.\n- [x] Recall is suppressed when the prior sidecar's `material_fingerprint` differs from the\n      current one and fires when they match — checked by a paired unit test that monkeypatches\n      `attest.current_material_fingerprint`.\n- [x] A recalled candidate reaches Pass-2 carrying the prior finding's `evidence` and `impact`\n      — checked by a unit test asserting the `_recall`-marked finding returned by\n      `pass1.run_pass1` has the non-empty evidence list from the concern.\n- [x] Fresh-finding verification is unchanged — checked by\n      `tests/unit/test_pass1_recall.py::test_finder_never_receives_prior_findings` and\n      `::test_recalled_candidate_dropped_by_pass2_when_resolved` passing without edits.\n- [x] The full local gate set is green — checked by `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and\n      `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"` plus `tests/integration` passing.\n- [x] Live validation: `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1 rebar review-plan\n      outrageous-uncultured-wildebeast` no longer emits the per-project enrichment finding\n      against the current description — checked by reading the resulting verdict and reporting\n      it on this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786621446985753001,"uuid":"e3219db2-aecf-492c-8cdc-ce9dc27a573e"}